1. sherpa-onnx
   - Upstream: k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx, Copyright XIAOMI Corporation, Apache
     License 2.0. No sherpa-onnx source files are copied into this repository
     or modified; the app uses a prebuilt package (see the last bullet).
   - Security note: the pinned sherpa-onnx tree carries an open upstream
     decoder bug (GitHub issue #3983, transducer greedy-search OOB write).
     Breaker mitigates per the Security Review audit: models are pinned to immutable release-asset ids and verified against upstream checksum.txt, and sherpa-onnx
     is kept off the server's network-exposed path [2].
   - The phone app's on-device speech engine is Breaker's own ASR-only build of
     this sherpa-onnx AAR (text-to-speech and speaker diarization compiled out),
     together with the other components it bundles (onnxruntime and several
     smaller Apache-2.0/MIT/BSD libraries). The build recipe and every bundled
     component's licence text are in `tools/sherpa-asr/` (see its NOTICE.md).

